            <ArticleTitle>Radicular compression due to lumbar intraspinal gas pseudocyst: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>731-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of sciatic pain syndrome is reported. Computed tomography showed evidence of gas in the spinal canal, and at operation a gas-filled pseudocyst was found in the spinal canal, without herniated disc. The cause of this unique case is discussed in relation to the spinal vacuum phenomenon.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
